/*
 * Declares the TemporaryType class.
 *
 * A temporary type represents an *incomplete* or *partially validated* type
 * produced during semantic analysis. It is used as a placeholder while the
 * validator gathers additional information (e.g., template arguments,
 * inferred closures, unresolved class references).
 *
 * Temporary types are never used to generate YIL nodes directly. They exist
 * solely to support the validation process and are always replaced by a
 * fully validated concrete type before code generation.
 *
 * A TemporaryType never borrows data and is never addressable, since it does
 * not represent an actual runtime value.
 *
 *
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::type::temporary
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/type/temporary.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-12-06
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
